  "body": "## Problem\n\nThe app kept suggesting **Day 1 (Legs)** as the next workout even after Day 1 was logged.\n\nRoot cause: `GET /api/current-day` and the log-workout auto-advance both read the `settings` doc with `SELECT * FROM c WHERE c.type='settings'` — **no `userId` filter** — and used an arbitrary cross-partition `settings[0]`. The MSAL → auth.romaine.life migration had left workout data (and a stale `settings` doc with `currentDay=1`) under a legacy `microsoft|…` userId, so that stale doc kept winning the read.\n\n## Changes (`backend/routes/routes/workouts.js`)\n\n- **`GET /api/current-day`** — dedupe by most-recent `updatedAt` instead of arbitrary `settings[0]`; coerce to `Number`.\n- **`POST /api/log-workout` auto-advance** — scope the settings lookup to `c.userId = req.user.sub` (partition-keyed); always upsert with `id = settings_\u003cuserId\u003e` so a stray/legacy doc id can't spawn a duplicate; coerce the day comparison/increment to `Number`.\n- **`PUT /api/current-day`** — coerce incoming `currentDay` to `Number` so a string can never be persisted (which would have made `dayNumber === currentDay` silently fail and `currentDay + 1` string-concatenate).\n\n## Data\n\nProduction data was separately consolidated onto the current auth.romaine.life userId (71 workout/soreness/cardio docs re-partitioned, the three duplicate `settings` docs collapsed to one with `currentDay=2`). A full backup was taken first. That fix is already live; this PR prevents recurrence.",
  "changed_files": 1,
